(footprint "TPS23730_RMTR"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "TI TPS23730RMTR, IEEE 802.3bt Type-3 PoE PD + high-efficiency DC-DC (ACF) controller, RMT package = 45-pin VQFN 7.00x5.00mm with DUAL exposed pad (PAD_G tied to RTN, PAD_S tied to VSS). Confirmed 45-VQFN(7x5) via DigiKey product page (Package/Case: 45-VFQFN Exposed Pad; Supplier Device Package: 45-VQFN(7x5)) and TI datasheet Table 6-1 pin function table (ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps23730.pdf), which lists 45 numbered signal pins plus PAD_G and PAD_S as two separate thermal/return pads -- matching this project's TPS23730 symbol exactly (47 total pins: 1-45 signal + 46=PAD_G + 47=PAD_S). Placeholder footprint 'QFN-45-1EP...' (single EP) was WRONG about EP count (real part has 2 split pads) though its 45-pin count for the perimeter was correct. 0.4mm pitch and per-side pin distribution (left10/bottom12/right10/top13) are an ENGINEERING APPROXIMATION -- TI's literal RMT mechanical/package-outline drawing (pin-by-pin XY table) could not be retrieved (PDF fetch tools returned garbled/binary content); only the pin COUNT, body size, and dual-EP topology are datasheet-confirmed. Flag for review against TI's actual RMT package drawing before fab.")
	(tags "TPS23730 PoE PD ACF controller VQFN-45 dual-pad RMT")
